<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Privacy' }) %>
<div class="card" style="max-width:820px;margin:0 auto">
  <h1>Privacy statement</h1>
  <p>This statement is issued by <strong><%= company.legal_name %></strong> (NZBN <%= company.nzbn %>), trading as <strong><%= company.trading_name %></strong>, the agency responsible for personal information collected through this service under the Privacy Act 2020.</p>
  <p>We collect the personal information needed to provide maintenance services: account contacts, site access details, site contact names and numbers, job photographs, and (for contractors) business, mobile, compliance and bank details. Card details for automatic top-ups are collected and stored by our payment processor, Stripe; we keep only the card brand, last four digits and expiry.</p>
  <h3>How we use it</h3>
  <p>To book, dispatch (including by SMS) and verify maintenance work, invoice and receive payments, pay contractors, meet our tax and health &amp; safety obligations, and contact you about your account.</p>
  <h3>Who sees it</h3>
  <p>Contractors see the job, site address, access instructions and site contact only for jobs assigned to them; job offers show the suburb only. Customers never see contractor bank details or another customer's records. Our hosting, email, SMS (Twilio), payment (Stripe) and accounting (Xero) providers process data on our behalf, some outside New Zealand.</p>
  <h3>Location data</h3>
  <p>When a contractor records arrival, completion or that a site is made safe, their device may share its location if they permit it. Location is recorded only at those moments.</p>
  <h3>Your rights</h3>
  <p>You can ask to access or correct your personal information by emailing <%= company.email %>. Financial records are retained as required by tax law (generally seven years).</p>
  <p class="muted">To be reviewed with a legal adviser before go-live.</p>
</div>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
